{
  "id": "REL-AUTH-02",
  "criterion": "`release plan --from-release-commit` fails with E165 and writes no output file in any of these cases: HEAD is not the given commit; the commit neither adds nor modifies the decision file; it deletes no changeset `.md` file; a claimed package's manifest does not change to its claimed version; a claimed package's changelog is unchanged; an unclaimed manifest version changes; or a claimed package is not found.",
  "is_error_case": true
}
{
  "id": "VER-CAS-05",
  "criterion": "Coverage: an exact spec covers only the equal version, a bare Cargo version is a caret requirement, a caret requirement never covers a prerelease, a Cargo `workspace = true` spec is tested using the root `[workspace.dependencies]` spec, and an npm `workspace:` shorthand (`workspace:`, `workspace:*`, `workspace:^` or `workspace:~`) always covers. A pnpm `workspace:` explicit range or exact version is tested using npm SemVer rules; an alias uses the range after its final `@`, and a relative path binds only to the admitted npm member at that directory. A catalog or other untestable spec is treated as covering and never rewritten; a catalog spec emits a CatalogSpecNotRewritten warning."
}
{
  "id": "VER-CAS-06",
  "criterion": "A spec that no longer covers the new version is rewritten to it, keeping the operator and precision for Cargo and npm (`^1.2` becomes `^2.0` for 2.0.0), or to the exact version for npm when `preserve-npm-ranges = false`. A runtime, optional, build or peer dependent that is itself released in this run, for any reason, has every such spec on a bumped internal dependency raised to the dependency's new version the same way, even when the spec still covers it; a dependent that is not releasing keeps its spec unless out of range. `workspace = true`, pnpm rolling `workspace:` shorthands and catalog specs are never rewritten by either rule; an out-of-range pnpm explicit range is rewritten while retaining its `workspace:` protocol and alias. A dev dependent's spec is rewritten only when out of range. A spec that cannot be rewritten mechanically, such as an npm range with spaces, `||`, a hyphen or a wildcard, is left unchanged with a RangeNotRoundTrippable warning."
}
{
  "id": "VER-APPLY-13",
  "criterion": "Outside an active pre-release cycle (`.changeset/pre.json` absent), after planning but before any write, `version` refuses with E121 when a canonical manifest's on-disk version differs from its version at `HEAD` and a changeset remains either in the `HEAD` tree or the configured working-tree changesets directory (including untracked files), or when a canonical manifest is staged in the git index but not yet committed. This detects interrupted applies without consuming retained inputs or stacking a second bump. A repository with no commits yet, a manifest/changesets directory that didn't exist at `HEAD`, or an active pre-release cycle (which legitimately reruns `version` without a commit in between) is never refused this way.",
  "is_error_case": true
}
{
  "id": "WS-ID-10",
  "criterion": "For pnpm dependencies, Callisto preserves the declared key, target distribution name and exact `workspace:` suffix separately. `workspace:`, `workspace:*`, `workspace:^` and `workspace:~` are version-derived shorthands; aliases such as `workspace:foo@^1` resolve `foo` while retaining the declared key; relative references resolve only to the admitted npm member at the resolved directory. Catalog and opaque references are not guessed or rewritten."
}

